WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.167
There is

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.969
a new museum in Charleston, South

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.237
Carolina, dedicated

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.939
to hundreds of years

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.374
of African-American history.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:10.043
It's black history in global context.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.611
And through individual stories

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.681
to show off the expanse and residents

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.815
of the museum's Center

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.584
for Family History.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.953
Researchers traced my genealogy

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.688
and I listen as a black man

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.523
with deep roots in the American South.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.125
I thought I knew where

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.926
my story was headed.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:30.397
I was very wrong.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.232
Very few moments in

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:35.035
my career have ever brought me to this.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.271
This is when it happened

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.039
at the International

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.240
African American Museum

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.808
in Charleston, South Carolina,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.410
which opens this month.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.011
Six centuries of history

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.746
packed into 150,000

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.748
square feet at the historic Gaston's

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.883
Wharf Above,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.218
40% of all enslaved Africans

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.820
would have come in through Gaston's

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.387
Wharf.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.388
We've been referred to

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.823
as the ground zero

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.658
of importation of enslaved people

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.060
into United States.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.393
Dr.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.861
Tanya Mathews is the museum's

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.831
president and CEO. A space of

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.500
solemnity

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.370
or celebration Yes,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.440
I refuse to choose

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.576
tribal art and contemporary fashion.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.011
Relics of protest

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.712
and reports of resistance.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.581
It's this infusion of trauma

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.616
and joy constantly

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.051
that we like to to talk about.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.553
Here you get the full story,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:26.920
but you're going

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.189
to get all the context in it.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.825
What arguably is the best illustration

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.159
of full context

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:33.893
is the museum's

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.528
Center for Family History.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.030
It's a team of researchers

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.965
with access to millions of records

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:39.632
that can trace

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.034
African-American lineage,

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.670
sometimes back to a slave ship

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.339
that came into this very port.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.373
The expert

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.441
genealogist here

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.010
spent months tracing my lineage,

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.246
and this was the day of the long

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.147
awaited reveal.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.916
Make sure you got a box of Kleenex by you

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.219
and sit there and enjoy.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.154
That's the museum's top genealogist, Dr.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.755
Shelley Murphy, on the laptop.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.423
She's joining us

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.091
from the University of Virginia.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.326
This is a tree,

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.194
just a snapshot of your tree.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.396
And I'm following your maternal line.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.698
Wow.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.399
That's a lot to see in

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.301
the tree.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.503
You see that box?

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.770
Well, that represents

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.038
David Vinny,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.741
my great grandfather's great grandfather.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.343
He lived in coastal Richmond

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.177
County, Virginia,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:24.844
on a farm

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:25.778
with his wife, Judy,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.148
and their 18 children.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.783
And in 1871, he filed this claim

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.851
to be reimbursed

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:32.719
for livestock

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.453
and supplies

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.155
requisitioned by union troops

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.723
during the Civil War.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.725
Another thing that is significant

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.128
is that he owned the land that he used on

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.397
and it was 23 acres.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:48.568
Where did a man in the 1870s

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:52.138
so soon after the end of slavery

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.474
get the money to buy 23 acres?

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.676
Absolutely.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.411
And and the thing of it is

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.146
I believe in question.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.814
He said he was free born.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.049
Well for some answers

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.017
we have to go back

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.787
more than 300 years to my great great

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.124
great great great great great

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:14.194
great great great grandmother Mary.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.563
She arrived on a ship in Northumberland

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.497
County Virginia

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.801
in 17, 12 before America was America.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.203
Her granddaughter,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.338
my eight times great grandmother

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.806
Bess, was with her.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.008
That's according to this centuries

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.843
old deposition that Dr.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.245
Murphy's team uncovered.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.746
Why a deposition?

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.548
We'll learn that a little later.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.016
And Bess at the time

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.319
was about 13 years old.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.453
Witnesses

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.455
apparently said they looked like

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.790
they were Indians.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.992
Researchers believe that Mary and Bess

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.327
were actually Mantovani,

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.194
like these people

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.696
of that region of Virginia called

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:50.730
the Northern Neck.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.000
We're not sure where they came from, but

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.704
Thomas Smith of Richmond County

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:01.174
did enslave one of Bess as children.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.142
And that was Sarah.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.177
And it's Sarah.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.246
My seven times great grandmother

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.281
who changes the trajectory

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.182
of her children

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.584
and all her descendants who followed.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.887
There was a law back in 17 05

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.624
that declared that all children

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.792
that are enslaved are free.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.861
Their condition would be based

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.863
on whatever their mother wants.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.898
Remember Sarah and Bess arrived

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.033
free people.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.535
So Sarah has a lawsuit

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.272
that's filed saying We're free.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.675
This is the actual lawsuit filed by Sarah

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.277
suing for her freedom

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.512
and for the freedom of her descendants.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.214
And that deposition,

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.181
it was from a witness

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.484
who saw Mary and Bess arrive

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:45.718
decades earlier.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:50.890
So in 1791, the court agreed with Sarah

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.991
and her children,

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:52.925
the grandchildren

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.194
and all of those relatives

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.030
who were descendants of Mary

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:00.333
and this are going to be free that

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.602
my ancestors

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.171
filed

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:08.041
and sued for their freedom.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.442
It is remarkable.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.376
We're not done.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.110
We're not done.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.513
And we're not done.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.681
Okay.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.915
We're not done. Let me get it.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.517
Let me get a Kleenex, doc.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.053
I know you have a box, Sheriff,

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.588
but not all of Sarah's family was free.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.791
Before the court's decision, Sarah's

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.693
enslavers illegally sold her

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:27.894
daughter, Rachel,

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.595
and then Rachel was sold again.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.531
And for the next 20 years,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.399
unaware of the court's ruling,

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.901
Rachel and her children

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.803
remained in bondage

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.639
when she learned of the decision in 18 07

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.140
more than a quarter century

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.108
after her mother's

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.377
groundbreaking lawsuit for freedom.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.646
Rachel filed this lawsuit

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.381
against her enslave her,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:48.781
claiming

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:49.415
that she was

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.017
the daughter of a free woman.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:51.751
And therefore,

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.454
she and her children should also be free.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:55.955
And guess what?

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.324
The witnesses and things

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.926
all came through,

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.994
and they were awarded their freedom

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:09.302
So what do you think

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.371
this is?

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.206
Oh man.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.942
To be an enslaved woman

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.010
suing a slave master to do it

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.414
twice in one bloodline individual.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.617
You're lying started out

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:27.520
enslaved and became free to up

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.422
and to where you're at right now.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.390
It became free

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.925
because those women fought for it.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:33.960
I'm going to tell you

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.663
what, Victor, the women in your family,

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.000
it's unbelievable.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.405
It fills in a lot of gray,

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.673
a lot of blank space.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.775
There was nothing there.

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.643
There was an assumption.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.479
Now, there are names, relatives

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:56.315
and places and stories.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:07:00.119
It certainly fills in more of the story

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:03.556
of my family's place in this country.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.860
I am so grateful to the people

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.594
at that museum.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:12.064
They spent months researching my lineage

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.199
and they've given me this book.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:14.967
This has the documents

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.235
copies of the documents

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:16.903
and maps

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:20.173
and death records and military records.

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.142
This is not what I expected.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.510
It is remarkable.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.012
It is not what I expected to ask you.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.047
What was your mom's reaction?

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:29.549
Oh, man.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:31.050
My mother's reaction first,

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.552
I had explained it a couple of times.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.587
Right, because no one expected this

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:36.289
And it

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:38.825
then started this kind of scavenger hunt

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.760
for details,

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.428
planning a trip back to Northumberland.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:44.163
Lizzie and Ron are still with us

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:45.832
to go and visit the Mattapan.

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:47.733
I mean, to know that

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:50.837
these women sued twice and one.

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.005
And in that day and age.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:53.406
Yes.

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:54.006
For a woman

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.975
but for a woman

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.743
who'd been enslaved to sue. Yes.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.312
I can't even imagine the witnesses

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.547
to come forward to support them.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:02.748
You're from strong stock

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.050
and that's for sure.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.852
It's the women in here during the break,

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:06.452
Lizzie,
that it's

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.353
so difficult

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:10.089
to trace the lineage of African-Americans

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.792
because for centuries

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.062
enslaved people were inventory.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:18.531
They didn't keep accurate birth and death

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.765
and marriage

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:20.800
for as much as marriage

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.835
was recognized or acknowledged.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.470
Those records absolute.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:25.605
And because of the constant

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.640
selling and reselling and loaning

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:28.374
and bringing back,

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.509
it was impossible to keep up.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:30.977
You know what's so brilliant

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:32.879
about the women of your family?

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.514
Set the law that you were talking about

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:35.348
was designed

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:36.849
because of all the sexual assaults

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:38.251
through all these pregnancies.

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:38.618
And it was like,

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:40.119
what do we do with these mixed race

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.153
children?

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.555
They created that law

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:43.689
so that those children

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.091
would be born into slavery.

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:46.425
The fact that, sure,

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:47.360
the women in your family

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.095
took that law and flipped it

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:50.563
and flipped it. Yeah.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.330
Brilliant.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.366
Yeah, absolutely brilliant.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:55.001
In credible research

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:56.168
and incredible story.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:57.970
And I just found myself wondering,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.705
with all the restrictions on curriculum

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:00.573
that are being imposed

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.508
in about half the country,

00:09:02.508 --> 00:09:04.510
it will become extremely difficult,

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.245
if not impossible

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.280
for many young people

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.148
to kind of learn this story

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.016
